// p91 — Sema's final method-call fall-through returns Any, not void
// (v5.3.5). Consistent with the Any-receiver / Callable-invocation
// policies added earlier — the class of "expected X, got void" false
// positives that showed up in v5.3.2 (`Any.trim()` → void) had a twin
// case in the final fall-through that was still using void.
//
// Now every unresolved method-call shape returns Any, deferring the
// actual type check to runtime. Sema-side `Unknown method 'Foo.bar'`
// errors for known primitive types still fire — this only affects the
// "we can't statically know what this method call resolves to"
// fall-through.
//
// The pattern: a decorator-desugared call chain where the callee is
// itself the result of another call, so its static type is (at best)
// Callable and Sema can't statically resolve the return type.

use sys

// Any-typed local — Sema pushes the resolved return through the
// permissive fall-through, and downstream assignment / arg-passing
// no longer breaks with "expected X, got void".
argv: List = sys.argv()
first := argv.get(0)               // first: Any (List.get returns Any)
second := first.substring(0, 3)    // Sema pre-fix: void → poisons the chain
                                    // Sema post-fix: Any → runtime dispatches

// Just confirm no Sema rejection; runtime is fine here because
// sys.argv()[0] is the program path (a real String).
print(second.length() > 0)         // true
